WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.250
Hey, David, both Biden and Trump are older
and have political problems that might prevent

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.740
them from making it to November.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:15.809
Who are the likely Biden and Trump replacements
if they don't make it to Election Day?

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:19.940
So we'll deal with Biden first and then talk
about Donald Trump.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.529
It's a little bit of a weird question, but
I I'll I'll answer it.

00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:26.679
If you don't believe Joe Biden is going to
make it to November.

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:29.939
I presume you mean because of his age?

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:34.230
Because I don't really know of what else is
going to knock Joe Biden out.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.910
I know that there are people saying he should
resign because he's been accused of sexual

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.090
assault.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.850
That's not really the way things work in the
United States.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:43.850
Right?

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:49.080
Republican, Democrat, for better or for worse,
in particular, Joe Biden's winning every national

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.460
poll and even competitive in a bunch of red
states that Trump won easily.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.100
You don't usually bow out when you're winning
every poll.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.330
So people who are, you know, using hashtags
about drop out Biden and this sort of stuff

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.189
for me.

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:09.140
Biden is on the ballot in November unless
he's dead or in a coma by that point in time.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.360
Now, maybe there are people, again, who are
thinking that the terror Reid thing is going

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.350
to make Joe Biden step back.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.200
I just think it's it's unrealistic.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.350
So if Joe Biden doesn't make it to November
because he dies again, I think that's really

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.070
the only way that it happens.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:27.700
It would seem natural that it would be Bernie
Sanders who would replace Joe Biden in the

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.570
sense that Bernie Sanders had the second most
delegates during the primary before dropping

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:32.909
out.

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:38.100
I think what would complicate it is if Biden
chooses a running mate soon, you would have

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.240
a debate.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.800
If Biden chooses a running mate and then for
whatever reason, cannot continue the campaign.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:50.049
I think he would have a fight between whether
the running mate replaces Biden or whether

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:51.890
Bernie Sanders replaces Biden.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:57.600
I think it would be horribly toxic and divisive
and could probably end up hurt helping Donald

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.600
Trump.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:59.600
I hope it doesn't happen.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.600
All right.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.770
That's on the Joe Biden's out side on the
Trump side again.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.100
I assume people are talking mostly because
of age.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.769
Trump's not going to be removed by impeachment.

00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:11.769
He's not going to be removed by the 25th Amendment.

00:02:11.769 --> 00:02:13.859
He's not going to be arrested or anything
like that.

00:02:13.859 --> 00:02:14.859
So.

00:02:14.859 --> 00:02:18.349
Maybe, maybe people think Trump is in his
70s and in poor health.

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:20.170
So maybe that's what they're looking at.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.719
I think Republicans go right to Mike Pence.

00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:23.670
I don't think there's any question whatsoever.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.280
I don't think there's even much to debate.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:32.510
I know that the idea has been floated of maybe
Trump would replace Pence for his 2020 run.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.880
Obviously, that ship has sailed.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.370
The Trump Pence 2020 signs are everywhere.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:44.099
Mike Pence has been made sort of a figure,
a prominent figure in the Corona virus task

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:47.390
force, despite despite being a complete clown.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:51.249
Trump has made him a prominent figure in the
briefings, et cetera.

00:02:51.249 --> 00:02:53.739
So I think it obviously goes right to Pence.

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:54.810
Don't see it going any other way.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:58.530
If you disagree on either, if you disagree
on what happens if Biden doesn't make it to

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.379
November or if Trump doesn't make it to November,
let me know.

